{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["And afterward He explained the categories of judgment — some among private individuals of the populace, some between a judge and the populace, and some among the heads of the people. Regarding the category among private individuals, He warned that a person not cause harm to his fellow in property, namely by saying: <b>You shall not steal, and you shall not deny, and you shall not lie</b> — for all of this concerns property. And likewise by saying."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The comment ends mid-sentence with וְכֵן בְּאָמְרוֹ ('and likewise by saying'), apparently pointing forward to the next verse or clause in the continuation; translated as the text stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:52.916624845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}